    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for a Hold on AMZN, and the evidence supports this balanced stance. Strong verified fundamentals exist \u2014 $18.99B quarterly operating cash flow, a $530.97B asset base, and a technically confirmed uptrend (price above 10 EMA, 50 SMA, and 200 SMA with golden cross, MACD expanding, RSI at 60.85). However, there is no income statement data to verify profitability, margins, or revenue growth, and the technicals are stretched at 19.6% above the 200-day SMA with a short-term reversal candle at the $198-199 resistance zone that has failed twice on elevated volume. The razor-thin FCF (~$1.13B, ~0.06% yield) is a genuine valuation concern. With sentiment, news, and macro data all unavailable in this historical window, and risk/reward roughly balanced (~5% downside to 50 SMA vs ~3-9% upside to resistance), the prudent action is to maintain existing positions without adding aggressively at $193.25.\n\n**Entry Price**: 193.25\n\n**Stop Loss**: 183.68\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current sizing; do not add aggressively. Consider trimming into strength near $198-199 resistance and re-entering on pullback toward $185.60-$183.68. Size smaller than normal given elevated ATR of 4.29.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
